From: NotaTV
Subject: [PATCH] httpd: restore index.html when only CGI is enabled

The "/index.html" suffix is truncated when BASIC_AUTH or CGI is enabled,
but only restored with BASIC_AUTH. With CGI alone, "GET /" sends an
empty path and answers 404.
---
--- a/networking/httpd.c
+++ b/networking/httpd.c
@@ -2784,8 +2784,8 @@
 	/* !CGI: it can be only GET or HEAD */
 #endif
 
-#if ENABLE_FEATURE_HTTPD_BASIC_AUTH
-	/* Restore truncated .../index.html */
+#if ENABLE_FEATURE_HTTPD_BASIC_AUTH || ENABLE_FEATURE_HTTPD_CGI
+	/* Restore truncated .../index.html (truncated under the same condition above) */
 	if (urlp[-1] == '/')
 		urlp[0] = index_page[0];
 #endif
